- How would you prune rarely-used branches to save memory?
- How would you support concurrent inserts and autocomplete in a multi-threaded environment?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to implement a standard data structure with array-based tree, index math, and clear complexity expectations.

## Key Concepts
- Segment tree
- Range maximum
- Point updates
- Space/time complexity

## Code Example
```javascript
class SegTree {
  constructor(arr) {
    this.n = arr.length;
    this.size = 1;
    while (this.size < this.n) this.size <<= 1;
    this.tree = new Array(this.size * 2).fill(-Infinity);
    for (let i = 0; i < this.n; i++) this.tree[this.size + i] = arr[i];
    for (let i = this.size - 1; i > 0; i--) this.tree[i] = Math.max(this.tree[i<<1], this.tree[i<<1|1]);
  }
  update(idx, val) {
    let pos = this.size + idx;
    this.tree[pos] = val;
    for (pos >>= 1; pos > 0; pos >>= 1) {
      this.tree[pos] = Math.max(this.tree[pos<<1], this.tree[pos<<1|1]);
    }
  }
  query(l, r) {
    let res = -Infinity;
    l += this.size; r += this.size;
    while (l <= r) {
      if (l & 1) res = Math.max(res, this.tree[l++]);
      if (!(r & 1)) res = Math.max(res, this.tree[r--]);
      l >>= 1; r >>= 1;
    }
    return res;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for range minimum?
- How would you implement lazy propagation for range updates?

Why This Is Asked
- Tests dynamic augmentation of a trie with aggregated metrics and tie-breaking logic.

Key Concepts
- Trie augmentation with subtreeSum and subtreeBest; O(length) updates; O(length) queries.
- Correct handling of weight deltas, insertions, and removals; lexicographic tiebreaks.

Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = new Map();
    this.subtreeSum = 0;
    this.bestWord = null;
    this.bestWeight = 0;
  }
}
class DynamicDict {
  constructor() {
    this.root = new TrieNode();
    this.wordWeights = new Map();
  }
  add(word, delta) {
    let node = this.root;
    const newWeight = (this.wordWeights.get(word) || 0) + delta;
    this.wordWeights.set(word, newWeight);
    for (const char of word) {
      if (!node.children.has(char)) {
        node.children.set(char, new TrieNode());
      }
      node = node.children.get(char);
      node.subtreeSum += delta;
      if (newWeight > node.bestWeight || 
          (newWeight === node.bestWeight && word < node.bestWord)) {
        node.bestWord = word;
        node.bestWeight = newWeight;
      }
    }
  }
  query(prefix) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of prefix) {
      if (!node.children.has(char)) {
        return [0, null];
      }
      node = node.children.get(char);
    }
    return [node.subtreeSum, node.bestWord];
  }
}
```

Complexity Analysis
- `add(word, delta)`: O(|word|) time, O(1) extra space per character
- `query(prefix)`: O(|prefix|) time, O(1) extra space

Edge Cases
- Negative deltas potentially removing words completely
- Multiple words with equal maximum weights requiring lexicographic tie-breaking
- Empty queries and non-existent prefixes
- Words sharing common prefixes affecting aggregate calculations

